      "description": "Watch Celtic vs Dundee FC highlights and goals from Premiership - Scotland on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 3, 2026. Celtic and Dundee FC locked horns in a highly anticipated Premiership encounter that promised tactical intrigue from the start. Both sides took to the pitch on August 3, 2026 , looking to establish dominance in a match where every small margin would prove crucial. A Cagey Opening Period The first half was characterized by a tactical stalemate, with both teams struggling to find a decisive opening. Celtic attempted to control the tempo through sustained possession, but Dundee FC remained disciplined and compact at the back. As the referee blew for half-time, the deadlock remained unbroken, leaving the fans in anticipation of a spark to ignite the contest in the second period. Nygren Delivers the Breakthrough The momentum shifted significantly just seven minutes after the restart. In the 52nd minute, Kieran Tierney turned provider, delivering a precise ball that found Benjamin Nygren in a dangerous position. Nygren made no mistake, clinical finishing to put his side ahead. This goal forced Dundee to alter their game plan, leading to a series of substitutions around the hour mark, including the introduction of Ashley Hay and Finlay Robertson . Late Drama and Final Whistle As the clock ticked down, the match grew increasingly physical. Both managers looked to their benches to influence the closing stages, with Celtic introducing James Forrest and Luke McCowan to maintain their lead. The tension boiled over in stoppage time, as Ashley Hay and Arne Engels both received yellow cards in quick succession. Despite Dundee's late efforts to find an equalizer, Celtic held firm until the final whistle at 90+4 minutes to secure the points."
